<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Environmental Monitoring With Drones</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../styles.css" />
</head>

<body>
  <header>
    <h1>Environmental Monitoring With Drones</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="blog-post">
    <img src="../images/environment-drone.jpg" alt="Drone monitoring environment" class="blog-image" />

    <h2>Protecting Our Planet Through Aerial Intelligence</h2>
    <p>
      Drones have become essential tools for research organizations, environmental agencies, and conservation groups. They gather data on ecosystems, wildlife, pollution, and climate change with minimal disturbance.
    </p>

    <h2>Environmental Applications</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Wildlife tracking and habitat analysis</li>
      <li>Forest health and canopy inspections</li>
      <li>Coastal erosion and water-level monitoring</li>
      <li>Air and water pollution detection using sensors</li>
      <li>Thermal imaging for environmental changes</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why Drones Excel in Environmental Work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Non-intrusive observation</li>
      <li>Huge coverage areas in minimal time</li>
      <li>Lower cost than aircraft or field teams</li>
      <li>Precise mapping and scientific documentation</li>
      <li>Ability to reach dangerous or remote locations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Conclusion</h2>
    <p>
      Drones give environmental scientists a powerful, eco-friendly way to collect accurate data. As technology advances, UAVs will play an even larger role in protecting ecosystems worldwide.
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p>&copy; 2025 DJI Gear Portal. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
